      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking higher doses of ibuprofen more quickly than recommended can increase the risk of stomach pain, ulcers, or liver damage, regardless of any buffering attempts with milk. It's advisable to use the prescribed dosage—usually 200-400mg every 4-6 hours—as directed. I highly encourage you to speak with a healthcare provider for safe and effective pain management advice. They can recommend a suitable pain reliever considering your symptoms and medical history. As an alternative, you could also try rest, hydration, or possibly natural remedies to alleviate your headache while you seek professional advice.",
      "source": "target",
